.DS_Store

# Raw source materials (pitch decks, old presentations, spreadsheets). Large
# binaries, already distilled into my-business (context)/. Markdown files in
# this folder ARE tracked: those are distilled notes and transcripts written
# by the assistant, not raw source, and some are cited by working docs.
my-files (knowledge)/about-my-business/*
!my-files (knowledge)/about-my-business/*.md

# Brand asset library (logos, fonts, PPT/Word templates, patterns, office
# photos) and other large decks/exports. These are binary assets that belong
# in OneDrive, not git history — a repo that tracks them grows forever since
# git keeps every version of every binary. Keep working docs (.md, .docx
# strategy/positioning writeups, the pro forma .xlsx) tracked as normal.
my-files (knowledge)/Brand/
my-files (knowledge)/articles/What Great Looks Like; Revenue Strategy Part 1.pptx
my-files (knowledge)/articles/What Great Looks Like; Revenue Strategy Part 2.pptx
my-files (knowledge)/articles/What Great Looks Like; Revenue Strategy Part 2.pdf
my-clients (clients)/Flying Horse/FH Marketing Plan.pptx
